= Uprising in Petrograd

Although we have secured tentative control over the city of Petrograd, counterrevolutionary forces are assembling against us. 

A group of military officers and cadets, right socialists, and other various notables, have declared an "All-Russian Committee for the Salvation of the Homeland and the Revolution". Despite lacking any real influence outside the city, they appear to be positioning themselves as an alternative government, and have received favorable coverage from a plethora of the city's newspapers. We have received word that soldiers loyal to this group have risen up, in an attempt to overthrow soviet power!

Meanwhile, outside the city limits, Kerensky has reemerged and has managed to rally an army to his side, joined by General Petr Krasnov. This army is now preparing to march on the city as well!

