@shut_down_newspapers
title: Crack down on the counterrevolutionary newspapers!
max-visits: 1
go-to: battle_menu
on-arrival: democraticity -= 2; elite_strength -= 4; middle_strength -= 2; elite_unrest += 2; middle_unrest += 2; labor_unrest += 2; left_m_relation -= 2; centre_m_relation -= 3; right_m_relation -= 5; centre_sr_relation -= 3; right_sr_relation -= 5; ns_relation -= 5; k_relation -= 5; rightist_relation -= 5; 

We take the opportunity to shut down many of the worst offending papers—many of which could be legitimately accused of incitement to rebellion. Although red guards successfully break-up many newspaper offices, we lack the administrative oversight and enforcement to really ensure these bans are followed, allowing many papers to simply restart production under new names. This infringement on the freedom of the press garners some criticism, but Lenin argues the move is necessary given the precarious situation. 


